From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 23:50:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] luma: Quick Options matches the Design Center

Owner handoff, 2026-09-18 ("Quick Options polish"): the shipped panel had
drifted from the design. Three shapes of control became two, holes opened in
the grid, every dropdown button looked different, rows that belong elsewhere
crept in, and the detail sheets floated over the controls below them.

Two shapes. Wi-Fi and Bluetooth (and any wired, mobile or VPN connection)
are the 64px connectivity cards; every other switch is a 44px utility pill,
an icon and one word, in a three-column grid in the design's order: Tiling,
Location, Warm light, Airplane mode, Keyboard, Cast, then GNOME's other
switches. A pill shows only when it can work (Keyboard with a backlight,
Airplane mode with a radio, Cast with a network or a known screen). The grid
never leaves a hole: two pills on the last row take half the width each, one
takes all of it, and a lone card spans the panel. An on pill takes the
design's tinted wash and stroke instead of the filled slab. A pill with a
menu toggles, and opens its menu from a chevron inside its trailing edge that
has no box of its own: 26px of layout, a 32px hit area, a smaller hover disc.
"Airplane mode" is "Airplane", the one label that did not fit.

One disclosure. The cards and the level rows share the 30px raised button
with a filled chevron glyph (luma-disclosure-{down,up}-symbolic; strokes
render as blobs in St). Volume states its output under the level ("48% ·
Buds4 Pro"); the microphone row, GNOME's own and shown only while an app
records, sits right under it with its input disclosure. Every level keeps the
disclosure's slot, so their tracks end together.

Attached sheets. A detail sheet is now in the grid, in flow under the row
that owns it: opening it pushes everything below down instead of laying a
second surface over the controls, and one is open at a time. The owner (a
card, a pill, a level's or the power button's disclosure) and the sheet are
drawn as one shape by QuickSheetFrame: the owner keeps its top corners, the
sheet overlaps it by a pixel, and the sheet's corner under the owner is
square. Its title is plain, in sentence case, with a muted count on the other
side ("Bluetooth devices", "3 connected"; "Wi-Fi networks", "5 available";
"Sound output"; "Microphone"); GNOME's icon header is built and hidden. A
choice is a 44px QuickSheetRow: an optional muted icon (device type, signal
bars), the name, the state under it ("Connected · 82%" from UPower,
"Not connected", "Connecting…", "Secured", "In use"), the raised fill and a
dot for the current one, and the whole row is the button, so the "Connect"
and "Disconnect" text buttons are gone. Settings links are plain sentence
case rows under a hairline.

Removed: the Notifications and Calendar buttons (they have their own
surfaces) and the background-apps row. The background-apps indicator is still
built and keeps tracking; only its row is not shown.

In high contrast the shared outline takes the high-contrast line: the dark
mode rules in luma-shelf.css restate only what luma-controls.css would
override, so the high-contrast sheet keeps its own lines and ink.

The panel's width is unchanged; only its height grows.
